<title>FRANCE: Lafarge to set up China plaster venture.</title>
<headline>Lafarge to set up China plaster venture.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>French building materials group Lafarge said on Monday it was setting up a plasterboard venture with a Chinese firm in Shanghai and that $60 million would be invested in the new plant.</p>
<p>Lafarge said the venture was part of a strategy of expansion in the Asia-Pacific region and that it would be the operator with 57 percent control of the company.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the main partner was Chichibu Onoda Cement with 38 percent and that five percent would be held by Shanghai Shipping Corp.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
